<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Perlis</h1><p class="st-meta">1843 CE – present · capital Arau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Smallest state of Malaysia, separated from Kedah by Siam in 1843 and ruled by a dynasty of Arab descent.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After suppressing revolts in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kedah-sultanate">Kedah Sultanate</a> in the 1830s, Siam divided the sultanate and in 1843 created Perlis as a separate dependency. Its first raja was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syed-hussain-jamalullail">Syed Hussain Jamalullail</a>, a Kedah noble of Hadhrami Arab descent, whose family has ruled ever since with the title of raja rather than sultan.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Perlis was a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing state on the Thai border, with limestone hills, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and a modest population of Malay farmers. It sent tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> and was governed by the raja with a small council. The royal seat was at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arau">Arau</a>, and Islamic law and Malay custom shaped administration.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-siamese-treaty-of-1909">Anglo-Siamese Treaty of 1909</a> transferred Perlis to British protection; it accepted a British adviser and became one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/unfederated-malay-states">Unfederated Malay States</a>. It later joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-malaya">Federation of Malaya</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia</a>, and Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuanku-syed-sirajuddin">Tuanku Syed Sirajuddin</a> served as king from 2001 to 2006.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/perlis.jpg" alt="Perlis" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Urmas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Perlis.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1843 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Arau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Syed Hussain Jamalullail, Tuanku Syed Sirajuddin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/malaysia">Malaysia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Perlis, Perlis Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=perlis" aria-label="Perlis on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7456 1935 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Perlis lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7776 2191L7780 2205M7776 2191L7754 1922M7776 2191L7823 2316"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7780 2205h0M7754 1922h0M7823 2316h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7776 2191h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7776 2191h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1934&amp;focus=perlis">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
